00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:07.020
Episode 2:
Hesitation

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.870
This year especially will be one of the most memorable years.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:39.370
You will be able to witness the Great Mission in person...

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.430
...so you should consider yourselves extremely lucky.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:48.000
189 years ago, the Earth came so close to extinction...

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:53.620
...but thanks to our ancestors, we are here now.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.810
But I'm so glad we are in the same class!

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.030
It was not achieved because of luck.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.910
Yeah...

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.830
It's nice to make new friends in the new class, but it's also nice...

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.370
It was because they were able to use their knowledge at the fullest.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.420
..to be in the same class with your best friend, don't you think?

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:08.200
Once human beings were fighting against each other...

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.400
So we are, like, way ahead of everyone else!

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.940
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.800
...for the name of race, region, country, and also for personal gain.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:09.750
Excuse me.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.680
But, by experiencing the First Wave, human beings have begun...

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.060
Will you be quite.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:13.940
Oh, yes, I'm sorry.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.400
...to walk into the new territory.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:17.940
She is scary!

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:22.210
The Second Wave will hit the solar system in a matter of a few months.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.950
However, this time, we will be able to avoid the tragedy...

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.250
...with our knowledge and courage.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.650
And I want you to go beyond the solar system with this experience!

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.160
Go much deeper into outer space!

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:39.880
Congratulations! And welcome to the Stellvia!

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:44.240
I would like to tell you this as well. Welcome to the Stellvia!

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.030
For one year from today, you will be getting ready to be a regular student.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:54.600
First language, second language, biotechnology, laboratory science...

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.680
...and spaceship maneuver techniques.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.780
You must select the appropriate classes according to your capability...

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.080
...and you must earn the credits.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:08.530
Besides that, you must clear these three tasks.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:15.010
They are: Theory of Knowledge, Creativity, Action & Service...

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:18.600
...and Extended Essay.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.660
You can never earn credits for these tasks just by attendance...

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.190
...or memorizing for exams.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:26.870
Actually, I can say the same thing about other classes as well.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.170
This is not a place for you to be taught.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.740
This is a place to study and think.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:35.170
Create your own future on the path you must travel.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.360
Oh, man, I can't make it!

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:00.470
Ah!!

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:08.620
Dies irae, dies illa solvet saeclum in favilla.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:17.790
Here!

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:21.110
Here!

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:23.490
Here!

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.030
13,587 plus 38,250 plus...

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:41.960
Whoa!

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.000
Ah!

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:01.140
I'm tired!

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:03.330
Here, take it.

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:06.040
Oh, thank you.

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:09.320
You already know her, right?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.280
This is Yayoi Fujisawa in our class.

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:13.320
Nice to meet you.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:14.350
Oh.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.260
Um, nice to meet you.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.800
This is my best friend!

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:19.310
Huh?

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.190
Actually, just a moment ago, we swore to each other...

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.780
...to be best friends!

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.500
Right now the price of my friendship is at a special sale price!

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.690
So, congratulations, you just earned the title of "my best friend!"

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.600
Well, making friends in our new class!

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.900
Isn't it so refreshing!?

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:39.190
What? But you said that the friendship is always "first come first served."

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:40.030
Huh?

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:41.360
What are you talking about?

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.240
Well, never mind.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:45.440
Huh?

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.150
Oh, don't worry.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:52.180
You can earn the bonus point to be my best friend as well!

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.420
So that means...

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:58.980
Surprise! You are now upgraded to my best friend!

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.670
Hmm?

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.640
You are funny.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.880
I was saved by Arisa when I was being harassed...

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.430
...in front of the vending machine.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:13.500
Being harassed?

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.980
Wow! He's so cute!

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.410
Wow! He's so cute!

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:31.990
Wow! He's so cute!

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:35.550
Arisa saved me from being stuck loving and petting that puppy...

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:37.340
Wow! He's so cute! ...endlessly like those two.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.240
It is an infinite loop of hell...

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.510
It does seem to go on forever...

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:42.560
Wow! He's so cute! It does seem to go on forever...

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:46.470
Well, well, today is the last day of the trial period of all the classes...

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.330
...so let's discuss our attack plan!

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.250
Attack plan?

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:52.810
We're going to analyze and decide which classes we should take.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:56.740
Oh, if that's the case, can I invite my roommate, too?

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.500
Of course!

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:01.080
This is Akira Kayama.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:04.120
Well, she is in our class, so you know her already, right?

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:05.620
S-Sure...

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.330
You look very scary.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.760
That's true. Akira always looks scary.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.500
You're always a little too serious, right?

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:15.240
Humph!

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.610
Anyway, why did they place this thing here?

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:29.770
Hmm... They've got nothing to do with the Great Mission at least...

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:34.420
You are right, because the Great Mission isn't a monster hunt.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:38.490
This is a spaceship rather than a robot.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.040
Yes, a spaceship shaped like a human being.

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:42.200
A spaceship?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.500
Once we succeed with the Great Mission...

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:49.520
...this will be used to travel! beyond the solar system...

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:51.190
...they said.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.100
Who are "they"?

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:54.490
Don't know.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:57.320
But how come...

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:59.550
...a human shape?

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.120
I decided the classes I'll take.

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:16.180
Some classes are my favorite, and some are my least favorite...

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:17.420
...but I'll make it work.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.330
Because my journey is about to begin...

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:22.450
Now...

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.200
This is your first space flight training as a preparatory student.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:29.830
I'm sure you all had plenty of training in the flight simulator on the Earth...

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:34.800
...but the Ora-avis Machine's system is far different than that.

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:37.320
Your Pilot Suit is also different.

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:40.580
First, read the manual word by word, then change into the Suit.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:42.810
Meet me at the hangar in ten minutes!

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:43.760
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:03.510
What's wrong, Shima?

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.080
Aren't you gonna change?

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:06.680
But this is...

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.220
Okay, let's go.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.420
I'm not confident enough.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:15.120
What are you talking about?

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:18.790
We are the chosen ones here, so let's have a little confidence.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.020
No, I didn't mean that...

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:46.660
Katase, you can't control Bianca in that after-the-shower outfit.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.280
But...

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:52.590
This suit is designed to protect your own life.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:54.520
There is no need to be ashamed.

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:56.960
The same to you all!

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:57.730
Take it off!

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:03.080
The cockpit of the spaceship isn't a bath or a shower.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.970
Now I want you to get used to the functionalities of your suit.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
Ten laps around the hangar now!

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:09.580
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.630
We have to jog before getting into the spaceship?

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:17.800
I'm sorry, it's all my fault.

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:22.310
No, Ms. Leila always makes you exercise before the flight training.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.390
This is for relaxation, so it's not a punishment.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:28.360
Wow, you're very knowledgeable.

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:30.390
I know.

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:32.120
Hey, you two, stop chatting!

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:35.440
All of you, check your pulse and blood pressure!

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:38.030
No matter what kind of circumstance you are in...

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.370
...you must know how you are.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:41.540
Hey, don't kid around there!

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:42.670
This is not play time!

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:46.050
Wow, she's so cool, Ms. Leila...

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:47.850
Is she your new best friend?

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:50.220
No, she's my idol.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.310
I think it's great just watching her from far away, I think...

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:00.250
I'm going to be riding that, soon...

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.170
You'll be riding with regulated G-force for now...

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:37.870
...but in an actual mission, there will be none.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.680
First, adjust your seat to your comfort.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:41.950
Set!

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:43.110
Set!

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:56.040
Welcome, Shima

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:56.080
Welcome, Shima

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:56.120
Welcome, Shima

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:57.330
Welcome, Shima

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:00.710
Your welcome.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.420
Welcome, Shima

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:03.780
Now, is everyone set?

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:04.990
Y-Yes.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:08.350
Your ID is already registered into your Bianca.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:11.940
From now on, your ship will be your trusted partner.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.800
Your height, weight, pulse, blood pressure, and other data...

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:19.540
...are transmitted from your Bianca to the control center to be monitored.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.310
So they know everything... I don't like that.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:25.120
For now, its power and battery are regulated.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:29.010
Don't worry, we covered all the basics.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.220
Start your checkups, and get ready!

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:31.920
Yes, ma'am!

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:44.400
Masaru Odawara!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.190
Yes?

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.500
Don't loosen up your safety.

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:50.420
Yes, but it feels a little too tight...

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:53.740
The hangar and your cockpit will experience zero-G.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:57.130
You can adjust your standing position at that time.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.320
Okay.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:01.820
Katase... Shima Katase!

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:02.630
Y-Yes!

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:03.780
Are you okay?

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:05.480
I-I'm oki...

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:07.570
Uh, no, I'm okay.

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:09.650
Take a deep breath and relax.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:13.350
Good.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:15.210
Gravity regulator, off!

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:25.990
B-1 class, the Ora-avis Machine Bianca, get ready for launch.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:30.880
B-1 class, the Ora-avis Machine Bianca, get ready for launch.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:41.290
Hi.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:42.820
What is it?

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:44.150
We are still in session.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.020
You saw it, right?

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.750
It's starting, finally.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:52.220
That's right...

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.150
Releasing the air, opening the gate.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:05.140
Releasing the air, opening the gate.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:34.410
First unit, take off.

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:51.380
Second unit, take off.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.910
Third unit, take off.

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.410
Confirm your position.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:11.380
First, check data.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.300
Adjust your standing position.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.130
How is it? Your first space flight?

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:17.280
Hmm...

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:21.220
It's real all right, but it hasn't jumped out at me yet with all this...

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:25.320
Well, that's as real as it gets flying through space.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:29.230
Actually, flying with your own eyes would be more of a distraction.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.030
Just believe in your monitor.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:34.130
Now gather around my Bianca!

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:34.930
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:44.940
That brings back memories...

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:47.170
Oh, they're doing it!

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:51.850
Well, it's about that time of the year...

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.560
...to watch the new students struggle.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:57.950
They've trained a lot on the ground...

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.790
...but this is their first time in actual space, so...

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:03.850
The Ora-avis Machine is a little different from a normal spaceship.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:05.440
It's a lot different.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.840
Um... um...

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:20.570
Good... As I expected.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:39.440
All right, well done.

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:43.270
It's hard to get used to controlling the ship while standing...

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:44.070
...but don't worry.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:47.660
You will learn this is the best way to do it.

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:48.990
Now...

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:49.870
Ms. Leila.

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:50.520
What is it?

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.110
Ms. Katase is still...

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:52.980
What?

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:58.440
Impossible!

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:03.790
Katase, what's wrong!?

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:06.030
Calm down, calm down, calm down...

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:06.030
What are you doing! Katase!

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:13.910
Look! There is something going on there...

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:18.930
What's going on?

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:19.980
I don't know.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.140
Leila can take over the control of that ship in case of emergency, but...

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:24.740
Hey, Leila!

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:27.360
Help her out for Christ's sake!  Stop that Bianca right away!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.180
I've been trying already!

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:33.710
What's going on?

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:38.490
It's okay, I'm doing just fine and nicely, Shima!

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:40.750
Calm down, calm down, calm down...

00:18:41.530 --> 00:18:43.730
Take a deep breath and relax...

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:47.800
Shima Katase...

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.570
Is she re-programming the navigation software?

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:51.940
Why is she doing that?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:54.420
I don't know...

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:00.060
I'll assist you.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:02.170
It's about time.

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:02.490
What?

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:23.230
You actually fly through space without looking outside.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:26.120
I thought I knew that already, but...

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.280
It's totally different when you actually fly...

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.030
Maybe too different.

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:39.970
Is it... okay to join you?

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:41.950
O-Of course!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:42.950
P-Please!

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.000
Hello.

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:47.310
Ah, hi.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:52.840
Ms. Katase, isn't it? Are you okay?

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:56.220
Y-Yes, although Ms. Leila gave me quite a lecture...

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:57.610
For 30 minutes...

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.900
That's why we were having a "Cheering Up" party!

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.300
I'll just get to the point.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.010
So what happened?

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:06.310
Um...

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:09.350
I thought I needed to do something, so I was deleting...

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:12.910
...anything unnecessary, then that's how it turned out.

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:15.980
Usually, it's impossible to unlock the control program...

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.320
...from the instructor's ship.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:20.650
No, I mean, I was just too busy trying to figure it out, so it just happened.

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:23.230
Well, Shipon, there is always tomorrow!

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:24.960
What is "Shipon"?

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:26.670
It's your new nickname!

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:27.090
What!?

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.500
Because your Bianca was flying all over the place.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:31.350
So you are "Shipon!" That's it!

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:32.910
What!? Don't call me that!

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:34.510
Why? It's very cute!

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:35.230
What!?

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:39.310
Shima Katase... She's no good.

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:42.110
She'd be a better programmer than a pilot.

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:43.960
Well, we don't know that yet.

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:46.350
It was her first time in space anyway...

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:47.690
Maybe next time...

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.250
I don't think she'll make it.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:50.670
Leila Barthes!

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:53.790
Oh, my. That's a tough one.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:55.790
I need to take a break.

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:57.060
Go ahead.

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:01.830
Think for awhile, yet still suffer.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.240
Now Yayoi Fujisawa!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.710
Sing!!

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:17.220
Yes!

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:19.180
Yeah!

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:25.690
There must be a way to tell you this in my own way.

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:31.470
I want to be natural and kind like singing a song.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.140
I want to be natural and kind like singing a song.

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:32.630
Akira...

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:34.830
Hey! Shipon! Cheer up!

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:40.470
Sometimes you may be stunned by the scale of this sky...

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:35.610
What!?

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:39.860
Here, here, here, here!!

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:38.410
Oh, that's good.

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:39.610
Rock on!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.470
Yeah!

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:46.920
...but you can't stand still in a middle of this busy world.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:45.610
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:46.920
Yeah!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
And still I looked up

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:07.070
Next Episode

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:07.720
It's me, Arisa!

00:23:07.800 --> 00:23:08.560
It's Yayoi.

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:09.590
It's me, Shima.

00:23:09.870 --> 00:23:10.890
I'm Akira Kayama.

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:12.740
Hey, hey, you girls are depressing!

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:13.780
You think so?

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:14.230
Humph!

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:16.470
Anyway, we are at the study group.

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:17.000
That's right.

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:21.010
Shipon is surprisingly smart, so we decided to learn from her!

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:23.050
"Surprisingly"? That's not nice...

00:23:23.350 --> 00:23:25.740
Maybe we can explore inside the Stellvia, too.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:27.800
Next episode of Stellvia of the Universe.

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:28.760
Hey!

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:30.000
"I'm sorry!"

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:30.850
Please watch it!

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:31.580
Well then.

00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:32.660
See ya!

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:35.100
Episode 3:
I'm Sorry
